        "search_text": "The grid operator, acting as a crisis manager, issued an alert and enforced a blackout to protect a 230-kilovolt line. This action, while framed as grid stabilization, laid bare the system's collapse, leaving a supply shortage of more than 950 megawatts across the energy sector entity's network. The power producers became the system's immediate casualties.",
