        "search_text": "When the grid operator imposed emergency control in the Visayas, it was in response to chronic system neglect and the failure of a single corporate asset—Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2. Officials then conducted load reduction, a measure exposing how the burden of crisis management falls on ordinary consumers to protect critical infrastructure. The result was a massive power deficit, with over 950 megawatts left unavailable.",
